  "adapter_allocation_analysis": {
    "original": "Each child produces a hashed-result record; List.map also creates an intermediate cons cell retaining that record, followed by a canonical-value cons cell.",
    "fusion": "Each child still produces a hashed-result record; the callback additionally returns a (canonical value, hash) tuple, and intern_list creates the canonical-value cons cell.",
    "extracted_ocaml": "Both tuple layers remain explicit: f x returns (y, hy), and recursive intern_list returns (ys, hys).",
    "interpretation": "The tuple layers offset part of the removed intermediate-list allocation, but do not erase the benefit: same-process pass-local allocation falls 2.1-4.5% with fusion. Native allocation-site attribution was not measured."
